take you several times.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:48.469
I know it likely varies from video to video,
but generally, generally for you, are you

00:00:48.469 --> 00:00:50.440
able to do it in only one date?

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:51.440
Thanks, David.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:52.500
Appreciate all of you.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:57.440
And yeah, I hope this place, it has nothing
to do with how long I've been doing the show

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.489
and it does not vary video to video.

00:00:59.489 --> 00:01:04.299
This show from the beginning has always been
a one take show.

00:01:04.299 --> 00:01:06.140
There's no cuts, there's no edits.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:09.420
It's all it's all there.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:14.740
And the only exceptions were we would do a
cut is if there's a technical issue which

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.400
tends to happen more during interviews than
anything else.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.970
There are sometimes situations during an interview
where we will lose the connection with the

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:25.110
guest on Skype and then we'll kind of like
reconnect and get situated and then we'll

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:26.230
cut it in some way.

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:27.230
So it appears seamless.

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:30.530
But yes, this is a one take show.

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:34.920
No insult to the people that do like the cut
up thing where it's like you film a line at

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.760
a time and cut it together with jump cuts.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:38.370
That's a style.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:40.060
That's not the style we do.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:44.960
And remember that this started as a radio
show where you're just live.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:49.000
So I from the beginning was just always thinking
of this as one take.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.440
So, yes, the entire show is one take.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:53.170
It always has been.

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:55.870
And I mean, I don't know, you know, you can't
predict the future 100 percent, but I can't

00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:58.710
think of any reason why that would change
in the future.

